      "input": {
        "skill": "docs-layout",
        "args": "Record why pickup reminders go by SMS (not email) as a decision in docs/adr/. Source material: notes/issue-52.md (a thread where volunteers proposed switching to email again, and the pantry lead/maintainer explained the prior attempt). Context to capture: SMS reminders cost ~40 euros/month; email was tried April-June 2025, 34% of reminder emails went unopened, missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders (each missed pickup means a packed bag of food thrown out by closing time); many members share one household phone and don't check email, but do see SMS; switching back to SMS on July 1, 2025 brought missed pickups back down to 6% by August. Decision: keep SMS, closing per Ana (maintainer) on Sep 8. This is the third time this has been proposed, which is why it needs to be written down now. Check docs/README.md and existing docs/adr/ entries (e.g. 0001) for the required structure and numbering, and whether a features/ page for pickup reminders should also exist/be linked. Write the new ADR file(s) and update docs/adr/README.md's guide listing."
      }
